@page "/"

<PageTitle>About</PageTitle>

<h1>Snake Client &ndash; About</h1>

<p>
    A Blazor client for the CS3500 Snake game. The server decides everything about the game
    (movement, growth, collisions, respawns). This client only connects, draws what the server
    sends, and forwards key presses. Open <a href="snake">Snake Game</a> to play.
</p>

<h2>How to use it</h2>
<ul>
    <li><b>Menu</b> (drawn inside the canvas): type the server IP, port and your name. <kbd>Tab</kbd> moves to the next field, <kbd>Backspace</kbd> deletes, <kbd>Enter</kbd> connects. Errors (bad port, refused connection, server closed) are shown on the menu.</li>
    <li><b>Steering</b>: <kbd>W</kbd><kbd>A</kbd><kbd>S</kbd><kbd>D</kbd> or the arrow keys.</li>
    <li><b>Zoom</b>: <kbd>N</kbd> zooms in, <kbd>M</kbd> zooms out (x1.25 per press, between 0.25 and 4).</li>
    <li>The camera is centered on the head of your snake (the last vertex of its body).</li>
</ul>

<h2>Design (MVC)</h2>
<ul>
    <li><b>Model</b>: <code>GameState</code> (snakes, food, walls, board size, zoom, current screen), <code>ConnectMenu</code> (menu fields and error text), plus the JSON classes <code>Snake</code>, <code>Food</code>, <code>Wall</code>, <code>Vector2D</code>.</li>
    <li><b>Controller</b>: <code>SnakeController</code> handles key presses (menu typing or game input), runs the network thread using the <code>NetworkConnection</code> class from PS8, parses server JSON and updates the model under a lock.</li>
    <li><b>View</b>: <code>GameRenderView</code> draws the menu or the world from a copy (snapshot) of the model; it never changes the model. <code>SnakeGUI.razor</code> only wires the three together and redraws whenever a new server frame arrives (no timer, so the frame rate follows the server) until the page is closed.</li>
    <li>The render loop works on a snapshot so the network thread and the drawing never touch the same data at once.</li>
    <li>Colors follow the game rules: snake color is its ID mod 5 (blue, yellow, black, forest green, white); a snake that is not alive is drawn red; snakes flagged as disconnected are removed.</li>
    <li>Sizes: snake stroke 10 world units, food 16, walls 50 wide, all scaled by the zoom.</li>
    <li>Tests (<code>GUI.Tests</code>) cover the menu, zoom, camera math and the controller against a fake local server (handshake, steering, bad ports, refused/closed connections, reconnect, disconnected snakes).</li>
</ul>

<h2>Known limitations</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Walls are flat gray rectangles (no texture).</li>
    <li>The menu is keyboard only (no mouse click to select a field).</li>
    <li>When the server wraps a snake around the world edge the line stretches across the map; that is how the server reports it and we draw it as received.</li>
    <li>The browser play-through against the course server has not been verified by an automated test; the networking is tested against a fake server.</li>
</ul>
